                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f2830aaf-0d0a-403d-8eff-deb50c3f90fd",
                        "source_entry_id": "5cdd395b-0f11-3377-ba32-9f01ba275566",
                        "target_lang_word": "splendour",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "splendour",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a9837c9-4f7d-3c1a-bc41-1c30cb731f79",
                                        "entry_id": "69c4aad4-9351-31ae-ad59-34e57103beda",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "British, Canadian, Ireland, South Africa, Australian, and New Zealand standard spelling of splendor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ccb8f38-d7c7-4514-a9c0-b5e2df530dc8",
                                                "sense_id": "2a9837c9-4f7d-3c1a-bc41-1c30cb731f79",
                                                "text": "If the kind of network we envisage is to be established, it would be unwise to begin any of its services hurriedly with older stock, which, however admirable in its day, now has an air of faded Edwardian splendour that is out of joint with the times."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2ded1862-f5a7-42da-9ae9-b28f0dbdbce2",
                        "source_entry_id": "5cdd395b-0f11-3377-ba32-9f01ba275566",
                        "target_lang_word": "grandeur",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "grandeur",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd1ee1c0-469b-30b3-9e6b-985e20315fd1",
                                        "entry_id": "b6f5140e-84f4-3518-ad89-dbb35bab470d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being grand or splendid; magnificence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b96e1fe-a732-4020-aea4-d4b73ea1fe7a",
                                                "sense_id": "dd1ee1c0-469b-30b3-9e6b-985e20315fd1",
                                                "text": "I wrapp’d myself in grandeur then,\nAnd donn’d a visionary crown ——"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ac835cd-b194-4178-803d-bf0ae0f5d2b5",
                                                "sense_id": "dd1ee1c0-469b-30b3-9e6b-985e20315fd1",
                                                "text": "So much of what followed from the drawing boards of others will have been designed with the demands, effort and grandeur of Primrose Hill [tunnel] in the back of their minds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b101be62-0430-4c4f-9a8e-a72e4f677c21",
                                                "sense_id": "dd1ee1c0-469b-30b3-9e6b-985e20315fd1",
                                                "text": "In a tightly choreographed ceremony filled with imperial grandeur, Xi and Putin then walked towards each other and met in the middle, smiling as they shook hands."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a38a491-dc4b-3902-9c99-d6f3f6a1153b",
                                        "entry_id": "b6f5140e-84f4-3518-ad89-dbb35bab470d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nobility (state of being noble)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
